**Given:**

Radius of first circle (r₁) = 7 cm

Radius of second circle (r₂) = 4 cm

Distance between centers (d) = 25 cm

**Formula used:**

Length of transverse common tangent (T) = sqrt{d² - (r₁ + r₂)²}

**Calculation:**

T = sqrt{25² - (7 + 4)²}

⇒ T = sqrt{625 - 121}

⇒ T = sqrt{504}

⇒ T = 6√14 cm

**∴ The correct answer is option 2.**
